  "Scenes.Maraescene.PromptFightMarae.SureYouWantFight": "Are you sure you want to fight Marae? She is the life-goddess of Mareth. This is going to be extremely difficult battle."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.RunFromPervertedGoddess.TurnRunForBoat": "You turn and run for the boat, leaving the corrupt goddess behind. High pitched laugher seems to chase you as you row away from the island."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.DeityGentlyAsks": "[pg][say: You return to my island, champion? What brings you here? Is there something troubling you?] the deity gently asks you."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.ExpressionFalls": "[pg]At this, Marae's expression falls. [say: I am sorry, champion, but I cannot do what you ask.] When you demand to know why, she quickly explains herself. [say: It is not that I am ungrateful or unwilling, it is that I am unable. Though you have stopped the assault on my soul by the demon factory, my powers are still vastly diminished from what they were. I fear I would not be able to help her...] Marae suddenly trails off, looking thoughtful, then gives you an intent expression. [say: Explain to me again, the ruins in which you say your friend has been living?] she requests."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.GestureOfRespect": "[pg]Making whatever gesture of respect feels most appropriate to you, you explain to her about Minerva and her condition, elaborating that you have come to ask Marae if she can possibly help you to cure her."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.PuzzledRepeatDescription": "[pg]Puzzled, you repeat your description, watching with bemusement as Marae's face lights up. [say: I hadn't dared to hope... a nexus! An untainted nexus, still hidden from the demons! Yes, yes I can help your friend, and you both can help me at the same time!] she declares joyfully. [say: Your friend's home is a nexus, a place of concentrated holy energies. If I can connect myself to it, I can increase my own powers and help heal her.] Focusing, she holds her hands only slightly apart from each other as a strange green light begins forming between them. It swells in intensity until you are forced to look away, shielding your eyes. When it fades and you can look back without blinding yourself, you see a gently glowing seed resting between her hands. [say: Take this seed, champion, and plant it in the fertile soil at the spring you speak of. Do so and I will be able to help your friend overcome her affliction.]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.StepIntoTheBoat": "As you step into the boat and sail it out into the depths of the lake, you focus on trying to find Marae. She may be Minerva's best chance of being healed. Thankfully, luck is with you and you soon find yourself pulling ashore at the lushly forested island where the nature goddess dwells. In response to your presence, Marae herself materializes from the vegetation, looking at you in a concerned manner."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.TalkToMaraeAboutMinervaPurification.ThankForAssistance": "[pg]You thank Marae for her assistance and gently accept the glowing seed. Stowing it safely in your personal belongings, you return to your boat and, from there, to camp."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.AfterLongerExamination": "[pg]After a longer examination of the remains, you see something odd. There is a pile of intact shards of bark. They look large and thick enough to be workable. You give it an experimental flex, fiddling around with it to gauge its properties, and find it to be remarkably strong. Maybe someone can work this into armor? However, there are tentacles attached, and still alive. You're not sure if you want armor that has tentacles in it."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.ClearlyShowsSigns": "Marae clearly shows signs of her overwhelming arousal and reels back."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.ConjuringFlames": "[pg]Conjuring your flames, you finish off Marae, squelching the tainted deity from this world. The fire rages on as the goddess screams, her tentacles shriveling and her bark crackling within the inferno."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.DefeatedAncientTentacle": " You've defeated an ancient tentacle-god. [b: Suck it, Lovecraft!]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.DeityShedsLayer": "[pg]The deity sheds a layer of bark, one piece at a time. [say:Take these and make of them what you will. My bark is powerful and divine, granted only to those I deem deserving. I need a long rest after such a battle. Farewell,] Marae says, smilingly peacefully."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.DivineBarkPlates": "[pg][b: (Key Item Gained: Divine Bark Plates!)]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.ExclaimsMomentsLater": "[pg][say: W-what!?] she exclaims. Moments later, the entire tree that was once Marae explodes into innumerable small pieces."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.FallenShortWayOff": "[pg]Fallen a short way off from the remains, a massive crystal catches your gaze. Your [eyes] widen as the realization sets in. [b: This is Marae's Lethicite!]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.LashingAtFallenGoddess": "[pg]Lashing at the fallen goddess with your infernal whip, you get a sense that this is quite a fitting way to put her down. While Lethice spent decades scheming to undermine Marae, you were the one that she should have truly feared. Now with Lethice's own weapon, it's you who lashes and burns the plant-goddess to smoldering ash. Although Marae can't help but moan under such savage abuse, the flames do begin to take hold. Perhaps she enjoys dying this way."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.MaraeSays": "[pg][say: You have proven an incredible warrior, champion,] Marae says, [say: I must concede, you are worthy of a great boon.]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.PickUpTheBark": "[pg]You pick up the bark and examine it thoroughly. It's unusually strong for bark. You thank Marae for it, get on your boat and ferry back to the shore."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.ReelsBackIncredible": "Marae reels back from the incredible amount of damage you've dealt to her."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.RightingWrongs": "[pg]Righting your wrongs, you plunge your shimmering blade deep into Marae's chest. There is a definite initial reaction as the sword shakes, but the goddess resists death. Steeling yourself, you push the blade in deeper, and wisps of smoke shoot out of the wound. Overcome by the blade's might, Marae screams in pain before fire finally erupts from her chest. The bark crackles and her tentacles begin to shrivel and die. The corrupted goddess is no more."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.RusticWayOfAn": "[pg]In the rustic way of an Ingnam citizen preparing for winter, you heft your axe and begin to fell the tree. Marae screams in pain as the first strike of your [weapon] sinks in, followed by another, and another. It's actually a bit exhausting trying to chop down a god, but you can't say that really surprises you. Following up the splitting of her logs, you wipe your brow and make haste to set her ablaze. Building a fire is nothing for someone like you, and it is rather necessary to ensure a certain demise to the fiend."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.SeverelyWeakenedNow": "[pg]As Marae is severely weakened now, you set about gathering the driest plant-matter you can to build a fire around the goddess. She attempts to growl her protests at you, but you silence her with a swift strike of your [weapon] against her face. Now squelched, she can do nothing but burn. This is the only way you know to truly assure her destruction. You work the kindling a little more, and, soon enough, the blaze goes on."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.SoWeakenedThe": "[pg]With her being so weakened, the best chance you have to finish the deed is here. You thrust your [weapon] into the chest of the goddess, putting the entirety of your strength into breaking her vile core. The wood gives, tearing and splintering, until you reach into the softness within. Feels like pulp. Marae winces and reels, pained by the severe wound. Her tentacles shudder and wilt, and you take a considerable amount of time trying to dismantle her while she is unresponsive. You aren't entirely sure if this will suffice, so you wipe your brow and make haste to set the broken goddess ablaze. Building a fire is nothing for someone like you, and it is rather necessary to ensure a certain demise to the fiend."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.TentacledBarkPlates": "[pg][b: (Key Item Gained: Tentacled Bark Plates!)]"
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.TentaclesBlockingBoat": "[pg]With the tentacles blocking your boat gone, you get into your boat and sail back to the shore and return to your camp."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.UnleashingFlurry": "[pg]Unleashing a flurry of punches and slaps, you barrage the goddess for several seconds. Upon finishing, you point to her and declare that she is already dead."
  "Scenes.Maraescene.WinAgainstMarae.YellsNothingBut": "[say: NO! How can a mortal defeat me?! This is unfathomable!] Marae yells. She is nothing but a twisted husk of what was once the true goddess. Although her power was still vast, you've proven capable of overcoming her."
}
